<section class="page-head shell">
  <p class="eyebrow">CSPC CCIT service desk</p>
  <h1 class="page-head__title">Queue rules</h1>
  <p class="page-head__lede">These rules apply to every ticket taken through CSPC Queue. They keep one student from holding up a line for everyone else, and they tell you what to expect at the window.</p>
</section>

<section class="section shell" aria-label="Queue rules">
  <ol class="steps">
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">01</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Who can take a ticket</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Students signed in with an account. Staff and office heads sign in to run a window, not to take a ticket.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">02</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">When a window accepts tickets</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Only on its open days, from its opening time until 30 minutes before closing. The office head can close a window earlier. The display and each service page show the current state.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">03</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">How many tickets you can hold</h2>
      <p class="step__text">One active ticket per service per day, and no more than two active tickets in total. Finish or leave one before taking another.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">04</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">The 60-second wait</h2>
      <p class="step__text">After you take a ticket, wait 60 seconds before taking another. Leaving a ticket does not reset that wait.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">05</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Your turn</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Staff call the next waiting ticket. If your code is called and you do not appear, staff mark a no-show. Two no-shows in one day block new tickets until the next day.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">06</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Leaving a ticket</h2>
      <p class="step__text">You can leave a waiting ticket from its page. Once staff call your ticket, you cannot leave it. Talk to the staff at the window.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">07</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Location</h2>
      <p class="step__text">The system does not ask for or store your location. You can take a ticket from anywhere. The limits above and staff judgement handle misuse.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">08</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">What the system stores</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Your name, student number, email, password hash, the tickets you take, and an audit record of sign-ins and ticket changes. Passwords are stored as bcrypt hashes. Sessions use one httpOnly cookie.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">09</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">What the public display shows</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Ticket code, service, counter, waiting count, and update time. No name, email, or student number. Staff and office heads can open a named ticket on the staff console.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">10</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Fair use</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Do not make accounts for other people, automate joins, or hold a ticket you do not intend to use. Staff can mark a ticket no-show. The office head can close a window.</p>
    </li>
    <li class="step">
      <p class="step__number">11</p>
      <h2 class="step__title">Questions</h2>
      <p class="step__text">Ask at the service window, or contact the CCIT office.</p>
    </li>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="section shell">
  <div class="action-panel">
    <a class="btn btn--primary" href="/">See service windows</a>
    <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="/login">Sign in</a>
  </div>
</section>
